          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most laptops, the Anker Laptop Power Bank with built-in cables is the right buy: 100W per cable covers nearly every MacBook Air, 14-inch MacBook Pro and Windows ultrabook, and you never pack a cable. If you run a 16-inch MacBook Pro or charge two laptops, step up to the Anker Prime, or save money with the CUKTECH 20 or UGREEN Nexode. Ultrabook users with slim bags should take the Baseus Blade HD.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Gaming laptops are the exception. No USB-C bank can feed one under load, so use an AC-outlet station like the EcoFlow River 3 and accept that it stays on the ground. Whatever you choose, match the wattage first, use a properly rated cable, stay under 100Wh if you fly, and buy from a brand that prints honest ratings.
